Select the ordinary unpledged game for unattended upstream stress tests.

Gooncrawl's newgame.cc:649-668 requires a pledge selection for normal games;
initfile.cc:290 defaults that option to "unknown" and therefore opens a menu.
The inherited stress rc files specify species/background and start their Lua
bots only after character creation, so fireworks stalls in choose_game before
any gameplay.  Selecting "none" maps to PLEDGE_NONE (pledge.cc:37-40) and leaves
normal gameplay unmodified.  Sprint already assigns PLEDGE_NONE explicitly
(newgame.cc:670-673); the arena scenarios do not choose a normal character.

Use the public early option so an explicit scenario rc can still override it:
initfile.cc:1590-1600 applies extra_opts_first before reading the rc file.
This default applies only to the upstream test runner, not installed launchers
or user configuration.  All scenarios, seeds, assertions, timeouts and test
exit handling are unchanged.  Do not quote the single-token pledge=none inside
CRAWL: the runner deliberately expands that command using shell word splitting.

--- a/crawl-ref/source/test/stress/run
+++ b/crawl-ref/source/test/stress/run
@@ -1,7 +1,8 @@
 #!/bin/sh
 set -e
 
-CRAWL=${CRAWL:-timeout 595 ./crawl -seed 1 -no-save -name test -wizard -no-throttle}
+# The bots require character creation to finish without an interactive pledge menu.
+CRAWL=${CRAWL:-timeout 595 ./crawl -seed 1 -no-save -name test -wizard -no-throttle -extra-opt-first pledge=none}
 
 run_one()
 {
